  "note": "Nominations were announced by V. M. Conran, town clerk, at Armagh City Hall on Wednesday 4 May: eighteen candidates for the twenty seats, so there was no contest in any ward. George Leyburn is styled M.B.E.; S. McVitty moved to this ward from the South-East Ward. Polling day for the urban councils was Wednesday 18 May 1949 (Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1949, p. 5: \"Polling took place yesterday for the election of county borough, borough and urban councils in Ulster\")."
